<title>DENMARK: Danish December reserves fall to 84.50 bln Dkk.</title>
<headline>Danish December reserves fall to 84.50 bln Dkk.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's foreign exchange reserves fell to 84.50 billion crowns at end-December 1996 from 85.0 billion crowns at end-November 1996, according to the central bank's monthly balance sheet released on Friday.  </p>
<p>DANISH RESERVES</p>
<p>				  Dec 1996    Nov 1996    Dec 1995</p>
<p>    Reserves (bln crowns)    84.50	 85.00	 67.40</p>
<p>NOTE - In a statement the Central Bank said its net foreign loans in December were 0.4 billion crowns.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33-969652</p>
</text>
